<title>USA: BP Chemicals in Indian licensing deal.</title>
<headline>BP Chemicals in Indian licensing deal.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>BP Chemicals Inc said Tuesday it agreed to license its fluid-bed acrylonitrile process to Indian Petrochemicals Ltd.</p>
<p>Indian Petrochemicals plans to use the process at plant to be constructed in Jageshwar, near Bharuch in the state of Gujarat. The facility, with an annual production capacity of 100,000 metric tonnes, is expected to begin operating by early 2000.</p>
<p>The British Petroleum Co Plc subsidiary said it would also supply the catalyst for the plant.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
